  "database": "rschema_0518",
  "nl_text": "The rschema_0518 database is designed to manage information about mazes, users, robots, and their interactions. The Maze table stores details about individual mazes, including their file paths and names, with each maze uniquely identified by a Maze ID. The User table holds information about the individuals who interact with the mazes, such as their contact information and names, with each user assigned a unique User ID. The Robot table contains details about the robots that navigate the mazes, including their current positions, types, and timer statuses, with each robot linked to a specific maze through its Maze ID. The Forward Sensor and Proximity Sensor tables track the status of the sensors on each robot, with the Robot ID referencing the robot they are attached to. The Timer table logs events related to the robots, such as timer events and their corresponding times, also referencing the Robot ID. The User_Robot_Operation table records the interactions between users and robots, including the type of operation and the time it occurred, with both the Robot ID and User ID serving as primary keys to establish a unique combination of user and robot.",
  "gold_question": "Business Requirements:\n1.Maze: Each maze needs to record its basic information, including Maze ID, Maze Name, and Maze File Path.\n2.Robot: Each robot needs to record its basic information, including Robot ID, Robot Type, Current Position, Timer Status, and Maze ID. Robot ID is the unique identifier for each robot, and Maze ID is a Foreign key pointing to the Maze ID in the Maze table.\n3.Forward Sensor: Each forward sensor needs to record its basic information, including Sensor ID, Robot ID, Left Status, Right Status, and Front Status.\n4.Proximity Sensor: Each proximity sensor needs to record its basic information, including Sensor ID, Robot ID, Coin Status, and Ghost Status.\n5.Timer: Each timer needs to record its basic information, including Timer ID, Robot ID, Timer Event Description, and Timer Event Time.\n6.User: Each user needs to record their basic information, including User ID, Name, and Contact Information.\n7.User Robot Operation: Each user can perform operations on a robot. This operation records User ID, Operation Type, Operation Time, and Robot ID.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0518.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0518\nCREATE TABLE `maze` (\n  `maze_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `file_path` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`maze_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_info` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `robot` (\n  `robot_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `maze_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `current_position` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `robot_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `timer_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`robot_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `robot_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`maze_id`) REFERENCES `maze` (`maze_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `forward_sensor` (\n  `sensor_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `robot_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`sensor_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `forward_sensor_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`robot_id`) REFERENCES `robot` (`robot_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `proximity_sensor` (\n  `sensor_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `robot_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`sensor_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `proximity_sensor_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`robot_id`) REFERENCES `robot` (`robot_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `timer` (\n  `timer_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `robot_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `event_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `event_description` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`timer_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `timer_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`robot_id`) REFERENCES `robot` (`robot_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_robot_operation` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `robot_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `operation_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `operation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `robot_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_robot_operation_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_robot_operation_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`robot_id`) REFERENCES `robot` (`robot_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
